     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I&#39;m making an module that uses some graphing functions that need RColorBrewer to work as needed. I didn&#39;t write the graphing functions and would like to avoid re-writing them if possible. <br><br>I&#39;ve been successful at producing a module that incorporates these graphing functions but it only works when I define the functions, palettes and modules in the same script as the ui and server functions. When I try to incorporate my module into a larger app I get an error message claiming that the palettes I&#39;ve defined (cc2 and cc1) don&#39;t exist. I think I just need to change around where I define my functions and palettes but I&#39;m not sure what would make sense.</div><div><br></div><div>Here are the relevant code blocks (note that &lt;PARAMS&gt; is an approximation and not to be taken literally):</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\"># DEFINE COLOR PALETTES </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># (currently encoded in the server component of my_Module)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">RColorBrewer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>reds </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> brewer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;PuRd&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>greens </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> brewer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Blues&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>yellows </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> brewer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Greys&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>cc2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">reds</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> yellows</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> greens</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>cc1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">reds</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> yellows</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> greens</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\"># GRAPHING FUNCTIONS</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># (currently encoded in a separate file that gets sourced inside of server.R before the shinyServer() call)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>my_graphing_function </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">PARAMS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  barplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beside </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> F</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cc1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> las </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> border </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  legend</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;topleft&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> legend </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rev</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rownames</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">order</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,])),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fill </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rev</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cc1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\"># DEFINE MODULE</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># (currently encoded in a separate file that gets sourced inside of server.R within the shinyServer() call)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>my_Module </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> output</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> session</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">PARAMS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  output$my_barplot </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> renderPlot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    my_graphing_function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">PARAMS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br>For the sake of completeness, this is what my server.R code looks like:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">RColorBrewer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># other libraries</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>source</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Modules.R&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># contains my_Module() as well as my_ModuleUI()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>source</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Graphing_Functions.R&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># contains graphing_function() as well as others</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># IMPORT DATA</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>my_data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Data.csv&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>shinyServer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> output</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  callModule</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">my_Module</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;NAMESPACE&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">PARAMS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Again, the module and graphing functions all worked together swimmingly when everything was defined inside the same R-script but as soon as I split the code into separate files my graphing functions can&#39;t find the color palettes that have been defined within the same module. </div><div><br></div><div>Appreciate any and all help. </div></div>"
